Body:
For the `maxContext` part of this request: it's already possible to override context limits per model in `opencode.json`. The merge logic in `provider.ts` gives user config priority over the models.dev snapshot:

```jsonc
{
  "provider": {
    "anthropic": {
      "models": {
        "claude-opus-4-20250805": {
          "limit": {
            "context": 200000  // override 1M default to save costs
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This works because the model merge uses `model.limit?.context ?? existingModel?.limit?.context ?? 0` — user-defined values take precedence over the snapshot defaults.

This isn't documented anywhere though, so it's easy to miss. It would be helpful to add this to the docs or the `opencode.json` schema description.
